From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fanasina RANDRIATSARAFARA <m.randriatsarafara.f@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Keep L1C, L7C and L11C
 on for the fingerprint sensor

The Goodix under-display fingerprint sensor is driven by the secure
world over an SPI bus Linux does not see, so no Linux driver ever
votes for its supplies. On this board revision it needs L1C
(vreg_l1c_1p8, I/O) together with L7C (vreg_l7c_3p0) and L11C
(vreg_l11c_2p5). With L7C and L11C alone the sensor stays silent
(chip ID error 1043, sensor not available 1064); adding L1C makes
detection succeed (224x192 image, status 0). Keep all three on.

The sensor reset (TLMM 41) is left to user space, which has to drive it
the way the vendor HAL does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
@@ -528,11 +528,18 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_AUTO>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Goodix fingerprint sensor I/O supply (1.8 V), see L7C below:
+		 * without it the sensor does not answer (chip ID 1043, sensor
+		 * not available 1064).
+		 */
 		vreg_l1c_1p8: ldo1 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l1c_1p8";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l2c_1p8: ldo2 {
@@ -576,11 +583,20 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Also the Goodix fingerprint sensor supply. The sensor is
+		 * driven by the secure world over its own SPI bus, so no
+		 * Linux driver claims it: keep it on, or the trusted
+		 * application cannot initialise the sensor (errors
+		 * 1043/1064).
+		 */
 		vreg_l7c_3p0: ldo7 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l7c_3p0";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3544000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l8c_1p8: ldo8 {
@@ -604,11 +620,14 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
+		/* Also the Goodix fingerprint sensor supply, see above. */
 		vreg_l11c_2p5: ldo11 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l11c_2p5";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2504000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3008000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l12c_1p8: ldo12 {
-- 
